<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian retail sales rose 0.8 pct in February.</title>
<headline>Australian retail sales rose 0.8 pct in February.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian retail sales rose 0.8 percent to A$10.49 billion in February, seasonally adjusted, after rising 2.7 percent to A$10.41 billion in January, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In February 1996, retail sales rose 0.2 percent to A$10.16 billion.</p>
<p>Analysts median expectations had centred on a flat result.  </p>
<p>Australian retail sales, February 1997 (A$ billion)</p>
<p>			    Feb 97  Jan 97  m/m pct   Feb 96  y/y pct</p>
<p>    Seasonally adj    10.49    10.41   +0.8     10.16    +3.3</p>
<p>    Unadjusted	   9.25    10.26   -9.8	9.32    -0.7</p>
<p>    Trend Estimates   10.38    10.31   +0.6     10.14    +2.4</p>
<p>Retail turnover by group percentage change, seasonally adj.</p>
<p>				Feb 97	 Jan 96	 Feb 96</p>
<p>Food retailing	     -0.1	   +3.0	   +2.0</p>
<p>Department stores	  +1.9	   -1.0	   -1.8</p>
<p>Clothing, soft goods     -2.9	   +0.8	   -0.4</p>
<p>Household goods	    +5.6	   +4.2	   -0.5</p>
<p>Recreational goods	 -1.7	   -5.1	   -5.7</p>
<p>Other retailing	    +2.8	   +4.6	   +0.8</p>
<p>Hospitality, services    +0.5	   +6.0	   -0.4</p>
<p>Total			  +0.8	   +2.7	   +0.2</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
